"<b>先说结论：</b>雅思口语的发音分占四项中的 25%，看的是<b>好不好懂</b>，以及重音、语调、连读这些发音特征用得自不自然。英音、美音、带一点中国口音都可以，不需要刻意模仿某种口音，把下面这些容易造成误解的问题改掉就行。": "<b>The bottom line:</b> pronunciation is 25% of the IELTS speaking score. Examiners look at <b>how easy you are to understand</b> and how naturally you use stress, intonation and linking. British, American or a light accent of your own are all fine; there's no need to imitate a particular accent. Just fix the problems below that cause misunderstandings.",
